.Dd August 28, 2026
.Dt BRFS.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm brfs.conf
.Nd BrFS replication daemon configuration file
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
file is the single source of truth for a BrFS node, in UCL syntax.
The kernel module never reads it;
.Xr brfsd 8
parses it and pushes what
.Xr brfs 4
needs via ioctl at startup.
.Pp
The following keys are recognized:
.Bl -tag -width "replicated_path"
.It Va node_id Pq string, required
Unique identifier of this node in the replication group.
Used as the last-writer-wins tiebreak: conflicts resolve by
(origin_seq, node_id).
.It Va replicated_path Pq absolute path, required
The replicated folder: an ordinary local tree on UFS2 or ZFS.
No new mount point; every member holds a full local copy.
.It Va state_dir Pq absolute path, default: Pa /var/db/brfs
Daemon state: content set, staging area, conflict quarantine.
The staging area MUST be on the same filesystem as
.Va replicated_path
(the atomic-rename requirement) and MUST NOT be inside it (a watched
staging directory is a self-echo storm).
A sibling directory on the same filesystem is the canonical layout.
.It Va listen Pq string, required
Peer listener address
.Pq Qq host:port
for the replication protocol.
.It Va peers Pq string array, required, max 16
Every other member of the group (full mesh).
Numeric addresses only in the POC.
.It Va psk_file Pq path
File containing the pre-shared key for the HELLO handshake.
The PSK still runs over TLS when TLS is enabled (defense in depth).
.It Va primary Pq bool, default: false
Initial-seed role: exactly one node starts with
.Va primary
set; it treats its local tree as authoritative.
Every other member starts with an empty content set and pulls via RESYNC
before announcing anything local.
.It Va rate_limit Pq integer, default: 0
Outbound transfer cap in bytes/sec; 0 = unlimited.
Parsed but not yet enforced (Phase 3).
.It Va tls_cert , tls_key , tls_ca Pq paths
TLS/mTLS for all peer connections (TLS 1.3 minimum, KTLS offload when the
kernel supports it).
Validation is DANE TLSA-first with the local trust store as fallback
(DNSSEC is out of scope).
All of
.Va tls_cert
and
.Va tls_key
must be set to enable TLS;
.Va tls_ca
selects the fallback trust anchor.
Without these, peers fall back to plain TCP + PSK (air-gapped mode).
.It Va tls_ktls Pq boolean, default: true
Kernel TLS offload for peer connections.
Escape hatch to force userspace TLS crypto if kernel TLS misbehaves on a
given kernel/NIC combination.
Requires restart.
.It Va events_drop Pq string array, default: empty
Event classes to drop at intake (selective filtering).
Valid names:
.Qq create ,
.Qq modify ,
.Qq delete ,
.Qq move_from ,
.Qq move_to ,
.Qq attrib .
.Qq overflow
is never droppable.
Dropped classes are recovered by the scan floor, NOT in real time; use
this to shed noisy classes (attrib = mode/mtime churn), not for content
filtering.
Changing this key requires a restart.
.El
.Sh SIGNALS AND RELOAD
Sending
.Dv SIGHUP
to
.Xr brfsd 8
re-reads this file.
Reloadable at runtime:
.Va psk_file
content, additions to
.Va peers ,
and
.Va rate_limit .
All other keys require a restart; a change to one is logged as a warning
and ignored.
A reload that fails to parse keeps the running configuration.
.Sh EXAMPLES
See
.Pa etc/brfs.conf.sample
in the source tree (installed as
.Pa /usr/local/etc/brfs.conf.sample ) .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr brfs 4 ,
.Xr brfsctl 8 ,
.Xr brfsd 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
format first appeared in the BrFS POC in August 2026.
